s an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can switch to the AND operator, enabling them to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2019-07-17T22:21:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:41:02+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#izettle-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"izettle-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:49:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-14T23:32:36+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"iZettle is growing its payments business in markets across three continents by using AWS. The company\u0027s payment solutions—some of the first of their kind to meet international security standards—allow individuals and small businesses to accept card payments through iOS and Android smartphones.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/case-studies/izettle-logo.c31835c43a2aeed1facf241601a739c9d6c44ad7.jpg","displayLocation":"Sweden","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eRead the iZettle customer case study, powered by the AWS cloud. AWS provides cloud computing services to hundreds of thousands of companies.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Financial Services","sortDate":"2016-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/izettle/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"iZettle","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2016","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"iZettle Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"customer-references#category#dev-and-test","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Dev \u0026 Test","description":"Dev \u0026 Test","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:47+0000","dateUpdated"